    {
      "id": "saltanovka-kolubakin",
      "nationId": "russia",
      "name": "Kolubakin's Division",
      "formation": "12th Division, VII Corps (Raevsky)",
      "side": "Russian",
      "summary": "Its Jäger opened the attack at seven in the morning and drove the French outposts back to the dam, but could get no further under the guns on the heights. In the afternoon Raevsky himself took the Smolensk regiment forward along the road; hit in the chest by canister, he stayed in its ranks and turned it on the French battalion that had struck its flank.",
      "notes": [
        "Raevsky, the book's named commander, led this division's attack himself; Kolubakin commanded it.",
        "After Nafziger's order of battle for the start of the campaign; losses since then aren't shown.",
        "The story that Raevsky led the Smolensk regiment with his two sons beside him was a patriotic fiction he denied himself, though his elder son was with the army.",
        "Commanders are at Staff Rating 8, the default for historical forces, except the book's named Lieutenant-General Raevsky, with his own rating; but 2 of the 3 brigade commanders at 7, as the list rates at most half of them higher."
